# What may never enter a build image: secrets, local state, and anything the
# images rebuild from source anyway.
.git
.env
.env.*
apps/web/.env.local

# dependency and build output — every image reinstalls/rebuilds these
**/node_modules
**/.next
**/dist
**/*.tsbuildinfo
**/coverage

# foundry build output and broadcast history — the seed container compiles fresh
crucible-contracts/out
crucible-contracts/cache
crucible-contracts/broadcast

# repo tooling and prose no image reads — except the one script an image runs at start, so the
# exclusion is `scripts/*` with that file re-included. It cannot be written as `scripts` plus a
# negation: dockerignore, like gitignore, cannot re-include a file whose parent directory is
# excluded. `apps/juror/docker-entrypoint.sh:19` runs `node scripts/seed-content.mjs --check`, and
# `apps/juror/Dockerfile` copies exactly that path out of the build stage, so with `scripts` listed
# whole the juror image failed at `COPY --from=build /repo/scripts/seed-content.mjs` — a service
# that has never been buildable from a clean tree, which nothing in the deploy pipeline noticed
# because deploy.yml builds `web api keeper seed` and never names juror.
docs
.github
scripts/*
!scripts/seed-content.mjs
*.md
